fishbowl@conservatory.com (james) wrote...

> Question:  Can an elf ranger ever get #riding skill?  I've spent a lot
> of turns on top of various steeds, but no skill yet.  

Yes. 

If #enhance doesn't let you advance it, see if there is a symbol next
to the riding skill indicating that you need more levels before you
can advance it. You get one skill slot per level, which you use on
your weapons and spell skills. You can use multiple slots per skill
even, so if you've enhanced a bunch of weapons and spell types you
might not have enough slots for riding and need to level up. Other
than that, it just takes a while of riding to get the skill.

Also note that riding a flying monster (or polymorphing into one)
allows you to shoot multiple arrows while flying, which is important
for a ranger. If you try it while simply levitating, you'll shoot one
and get pushed in the oposite direction by the recoil, so you stop
shooting.

> If I can get
> basic, will I be able to pick stuff up off the ground?

Yes.


But you can't eat off the ground. (but you can tin off the ground).
This is somewhat important if you end up riding a dragon, as it'll eat
most of the corpses you can't pick up (you have 1 turn to pick it up)
or you have to dismount. Bring emergency food and a ring of slow
digestion if going this way.


Other stuff: learn (and keep fresh) some healing spells as you can't
heal your steed with potions while riding it. There's also a problem
with being unable to dismount if the saddle gets cursed. I think
scrolls of remove curse might fix that, but I'm not sure.

That was basically my riding experience from my last elven ranger. HTH

